LIGHT — the photonic programming language — is Thomas Frumkin's work.
The original: https://github.com/teslasolar/light (created 2026-08-05; package.json declares MIT, author Thomas Frumkin).
This repository is the AI-Native Solutions estate's fork of it, used with permission and kept in step with the original.
Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin.

The estate uses LIGHT as the runtime under the Konomi Tongue (https://github.com/sjgant80-hub/konomi-tongue): its prime-indexed
opcodes, rings and buses feed the Tongue's legend, and its templates (a whole program called by name) are the model for the
Tongue's shared dictionary.
